WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:09.740
Today's theme is holiness and the body.

2
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.520
Four things you need to know about holiness and the body. Ready?

3
00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:13.740
If you're taking notes, number one,

4
00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:18.450
God's call to holiness isn't just to your spirit,

5
00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.760
it's to your body as well. Now, this is very clear from

6
00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:26.680
scripture. It's literally all over the New Testament. Let me quote a few for you.

7
00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:30.080
All right? "Don't you know that your body is a temple of the Holy Spirit?" 1

8
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.040
Corinthians. "I pray God your whole spirit and soul and body be preserved

9
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.120
blameless." 1 Thessalonians, chapter five.

10
00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.380
"Cleanse yourselves of all filthiness of flesh and spirit."

11
00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.949
2 Corinthians, chapter seven. "Offer your bodies a living sacrifice, holy and

12
00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:48.740
acceptable." Romans 12. "Don't let sin reign in your mortal body so you

13
00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:52.620
obey it in its desires." Romans six. Are you convinced yet? All right.

14
00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:54.780
I want you to notice how practical holiness is.

15
00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.720
God recognizes that you're not just a spirit, you have a body.

16
00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:03.200
He's not giving you some mystical experience that doesn't touch where you

17
00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:07.010
actually live. Holiness is really where it's

18
00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:09.900
practical and the rubber meets the road in your life.

19
00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.640
I want you to note that the body is called to be a part of the

20
00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:16.080
project of holiness. It's not irrelevant to it.

21
00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:20.220
In the early church, there was a Gnostic heresy that said that matter was

22
00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.760
lesser and evil and only spirit was pure.

23
00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:27.420
And Gnostic teachers compared the spirit actually to a jewel located in the pigpen

24
00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:27.960
of the body.

25
00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:32.880
Some of them even taught that Jesus didn't have a physical body because they

26
00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:36.510
thought that having matter, having a physical body would've made him

27
00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:39.580
impure. You know what? That's hogwash.

28
00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:44.160
God's call to holiness is to your spirit and to the body you

29
00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:47.700
have. Having a body is no reason you can't be holy.

30
00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:51.600
Paul even says, "Whether you eat or drink or whatever you

31
00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:54.400
do, do it all to the glory of God."

32
00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:58.800
So if you've just kind of lived your whole life assuming you're always going to be

33
00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:02.740
defeated by the urges of your body, then you need to understand that God has a call

34
00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:06.600
to holiness for you. God knows you live in a body, and he

35
00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:09.820
created this physical flesh with a purpose and with a

36
00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:13.250
potential to be holy. When you are raised

37
00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:17.800
in the new heavens and new Earth, you'll have a glorified body, and it'll still be

38
00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:21.540
a body of actual flesh like the one Jesus has now, and he ate

39
00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:23.549
broiled fish with his disciples. Right?

40
00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:28.120
God is so mighty that he can produce holiness even in a

41
00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:32.109
person that's limited by an actual physical body like yours.

42
00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:36.510
Number two, bodily drives and temptations are not

43
00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:39.340
incompatible with holiness. While God

44
00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:43.680
calls you to holiness in your body, it's important to

45
00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:47.640
understand that holiness is not physical perfection or immunity

46
00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.300
to temptation. Our physical bodies have been affected by the fall,

47
00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:53.980
but they in themselves are not sinful.

48
00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:58.740
Physical drives for food and rest and drink and sex

49
00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:00.470
are not incompatible with holiness.

50
00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:04.480
Jesus had all of those, and he's a perfect example of

51
00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:08.460
holiness. Jesus got tired. Jesus needed food. Jesus got hungry.

52
00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:12.090
He got thirsty. He was tempted in all the same ways that we are,

53
00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:14.859
but he didn't sin. He lived in holiness.

54
00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:19.060
So if you're tracking with me here, temptations to sin are

55
00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:22.800
not incompatible with holiness. Jesus was tempted, and he's

56
00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:26.760
a perfect example of holiness. So track

57
00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:30.440
with me. Temptation isn't sin. Noticing isn't sin.

58
00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:34.320
Even attraction isn't sin. You think Jesus was attracted by the

59
00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:37.380
idea of bread after fasting 40 days in the wilderness?

60
00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:40.970
You think he was attracted to the idea of not dying on the cross even though it was

61
00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:44.100
the will of the Father for him? You better believe it.

62
00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:47.760
Sin comes not when we notice or when we're tempted or even attracted to something

63
00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:49.960
that wouldn't be God's will for us.

64
00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:54.710
Sin comes when we choose what we know is not holy.

65
00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:56.240
Number three,

66
00:03:57.410 --> 00:04:01.100
holiness in the body is about surrender followed by

67
00:04:01.109 --> 00:04:04.500
discipline. The Bible is very clear that our bodies should be

68
00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:08.370
surrendered to holiness. Right? In a lot of

69
00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.620
people, the body rules over the mind.

70
00:04:11.329 --> 00:04:14.720
And for some people, it's like there's no gap between instinct and response.

71
00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.839
And the smaller that gap between instinct and response is, the more like the

72
00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:21.731
animals we are. Right? You need to surrender your body to the Lord and

73
00:04:21.731 --> 00:04:25.400
ask him to help you to install a gap between your instincts and

74
00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:29.040
drives and responses, a gap in which your

75
00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:32.890
purified, empowered mind and will can

76
00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:36.680
activate and come into play. Learning to create and use that gap

77
00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:38.850
between instinct and response is self-discipline.

78
00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:43.180
Paul said, "I strike a blow to my body and make it my slave

79
00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:47.380
so that after I have preached to others, I myself will not be

80
00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:50.680
disqualified for the prize." Self-discipline.

81
00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:54.520
Number four, your body can be holy while you're waiting for

82
00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:55.400
redemption. Now, remember,

83
00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:57.680
put on your possibility glasses here.

84
00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:02.220
God would not issue a call to your physical body to holiness

85
00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:06.300
if he was not willing to create it in you or not able.

86
00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:10.700
Dr. Phil Brown says, "God who knows our frame and empowers our inner

87
00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:13.560
life will not command the impossible."

88
00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:18.220
Someday, your body will be delivered from the effects of sin and set free

89
00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:22.060
to glorious perfection. But for now, you can live in holiness

90
00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:25.480
if you'll capture those drives, understand temptation's

91
00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:28.980
limitations, and discipline your body while you're

92
00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:30.340
waiting for redemption.

93
00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:31.800
I'll see you tomorrow.
